abstract: >-
  Rigorous interval-arithmetic certificate for the first 40,000 decimal
  digits of the Golomb-Dickman constant
  lambda = integral_0^infinity exp(-u - E_1(u)) du. The certificate gives
  integers Lambda_- < Lambda_+ and a scale S = 133074 such that
  lambda lies in [Lambda_-/2^S, Lambda_+/2^S] and
  floor(10^40000 Lambda_-/2^S) = floor(10^40000 Lambda_+/2^S); the digits
  are therefore proved by truncation. The interval width is about
  10^-40042.26, leaving roughly 42 guard digits. The package also contains
  a dependency-free checker, the producing code, the published checkpoints,
  and an OEIS b-file for A084945 with terms n = 0..39999.
